  "application_type_full": "Full planning permission",
  "description": "Ground floor rear extension and internal reconfiguration including side infill, courtyard, and internal alterations to improve spatial layout.\nThis application proposes: \n• A single-storey ground floor rear extension and side infill, \nincorporating a flat roof with Velux-style rooflights and a sloped roof \nto the infill portion. \n• Large glazed metal bifolding doors to open up the rear elevation \nand improve garden access. \n• Reconfiguration of internal spaces, including: \n• Conversion of the existing reception into a bedroom. \n• Repurposing of the existing kitchen into a study. \n• Relocation of circulation via a new hallway, with integrated cloak \nstorage and access to a new utility room. \n• The former Bedroom 1 is incorporated into the rear extension and \ntransformed into part of a new open-plan living/kitchen/dining area. \n• A central courtyard is introduced within the infill to provide natural \nlight to Bedroom 2 and the new study. \n• The rear facade will be constructed using London stock brick to \nmatch the original building fabric. \n• All front-facing windows will be replaced with like-for-like designs in \nkeeping with the original architectural rhythm. \n• A step down from the hallway to the new rear space is proposed; \nthe existing garden step will remain. \n• Refer to proposed drawings: PL100B, PL101A, PL102, PL103A, PL104, \nPL106. \nExisting drawings include: EX01B, EX02, EX03, EX04A, EX05, EX06.",
